course: dictionary
lesson: 9465
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word starter can be a dish, a person, a machine part, or a mixture for bread. Look at the words around it first, then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: «Many early cars were started by turning a starting handle at the front; electric starters only came in from about 1912.» The clues are cars, started and engines, so a starter here is a device that starts an engine. Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: a device that starts an engine still makes sense.
explain: In «Sourdough uses wild yeast and bacteria... a starter can be kept alive and fed for many years», the clues are fed and kept alive, not food on a plate. So a sourdough starter is a mixture of yeast and bacteria that you keep going to make bread. When the clues do not settle it, check a dictionary.
fact: Starter is a noun, and its plural is starters.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, a starter is a small dish eaten first in a meal; in the US it is called an appetizer.
fact: A starter can also be a person who starts a race, or a device that starts an engine.
fact: «For starters» is an informal phrase that means to begin with, or first of all.
fact: A «sourdough starter» is a mixture of wild yeast and bacteria that can be kept alive and fed for many years.
exercise: «Electric starters only came in from about 1912.» What does starter mean in this sentence? | A mixture of yeast used for bread | A small dish eaten before a meal | A person who starts a race | *A device that starts an engine
exercise: «We ordered a starter of soup before the main course.» What does starter mean here? | A bread mixture kept alive | A person who starts a race | *A small dish eaten first in a meal | A device that starts an engine
exercise: «For starters, let's tidy the room.» What does for starters mean? | Only just | Very quickly | *To begin with, first of all | Finally, at the end
test: «The starter fired the gun and the runners sprinted off.» What does starter mean in this sentence? | A small dish eaten first | *A person who starts a race | A mixture of yeast and bacteria | A device that starts an engine
test: «A sourdough starter can be fed for many years.» What is a sourdough starter? | *A mixture of wild yeast and bacteria, kept alive to make bread | A person who begins a game | A machine that starts a car | A small dish eaten at the start of a meal
exam: Read «Sourdough uses wild yeast and bacteria; the bacteria make acids that give the sour taste.» Which meaning of starter fits the sentence? | A device that starts an engine | A person who starts a race | A small dish eaten first in a meal | *A mixture of wild yeast and bacteria used to make bread
